# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# production
/build
/logs
/public/dist

# Capacitor native projects — generated by `npm run cap:add:android`/`:ios`
# (see DEPLOY_MOBILE.md) on whichever machine actually has Android
# Studio/Xcode; regenerable from capacitor.config.json, not source.
/android
/ios

# electron-builder output (installers/binaries per platform)
/dist-electron

# Downloadable app packages served by public/download.html. The two thin
# PWABuilder wrappers (.apk ~1MB, the Windows .zip ~1MB) ARE committed — at
# that size they cost nothing and a plain `git pull` deploy puts them on the
# server for free. The Electron desktop builds are a different story: they
# bundle all of Chromium, so Shalter.AppImage is ~119MB — past GitHub's hard
# 100MB-per-file limit, which would make the push itself fail — and the
# ~82MB .deb would balloon this 11MB repo permanently (git history never
# forgets a blob). Both are reproducible with `npm run electron:build:linux`
# and get onto the server via scripts/upload-downloads.sh instead.
/public/downloads/*.AppImage
/public/downloads/*.deb
/public/downloads/*.dmg
/public/downloads/*.exe

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*
# ...but the template with no secrets in it belongs in the repo, otherwise
# nobody deploying this knows which variables exist.
!.env.example

# runtime SQLite database — this is user data (accounts, messages, calls...),
# not source; the old flat-JSON-file equivalents got committed by mistake in
# this repo's history, don't repeat that with a binary DB file (no meaningful
# diffs, bloats the repo, and it's real user data besides). See DEPLOY.md for
# the actual persistence story (mount /app/data as a volume).
/data/*.db
/data/*.db-wal
/data/*.db-shm
# Uploaded attachments (server/routes/uploads.js) — user data, and gigabytes of it.
/data/uploads/
# Letters written when SMTP isn't configured (server/lib/mailer.js). They hold
# one-time recovery codes in plain text — never commit them.
/data/outbox/
